e constant  term as well is the correct one so of  course this answer is what we had found  in  the past to be the optimal the least  mean squares estimator of X as we  discussed earlier when this is linear in  X it has to be the same as the linear  least mean squares estimator so this  answer is not a surprise but it was an  interesting and perhaps useful exercise  to go through the details of this  calculation to see what it takes to  figure out the different terms in this  formula
 

